{title: 034 - Wake the Song}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #034 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 34}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Wake the song of [Bb]joy and [F]gladness; Hither [C]bring your [G7]noblest [C]lays;
[C7]Banish [F]every [Bb]thought of [F]sadness, Pouring forth [Bb]your [F]high[C7]est [F]praise.
[F]Sing to [C]Him whose care has [C7]brought us Once a[Dm]gain [C]with [F]friends [G7]to [C]meet,
[C]And whose [F]lov[C7]ing [Dm]voice [A]has [Bb]taught us Of the [F]way to Je[C7]sus' [F]feet.
[x]Wake the song, ([C]wake the song,) [x]wake the song, ([F]wake the song,)
[F]the [Bb]song of joy and [F]gladness,
[x]Wake the song, ([F]wake the song,) [x]wake the song, ([Bb]wake the song,)
[C]The [F]song [Bb]of [F]Ju[C7]bi[F]lee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]Wake [Bb]the [F]song, [C]wake [G7]the [C]song,
[C7][F]The [Bb]song [F]of [Bb][F]joy [C7]and [F]gladness,
[F][C]Wake [C7]the [Dm]song, [C][F]wake [G7]the [C]song,
[C][F][C7]The [Dm][A]song [Bb][F]of [C7][F]Jubilee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F][Bb]Joyfully [F]with [C]songs [G7]and [C]banners,
[C7][F]We [Bb]will [F]greet [Bb][F]the [C7]festal [F]day;
[F][C]Shout [C7][Dm]aloud [C]our [F][G7]glad [C]hosannas,
[C][F]And [C7][Dm]our [A][Bb]grateful [F][C7]homage [F]pay.
[x]We [C]will chant [x]our [F]Savior's glory
[F]while our [Bb]thoughts we [F]raise above,
[x]Telling [F]still the [x]old, [Bb]old, story,
[C][F]Precious [Bb]theme- [F][C7]redeeming [F]love!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Thanks [Bb]to [F]Thee, [C]O [G7]holy [C]Father,
[C7][F]For [Bb]the [F]mercies [Bb][F]of [C7]the [F]year;
[F][C]May [C7]each [Dm]heart, [C]as [F]here [G7]we [C]gather,
[C][F][C7]Swell [Dm][A]with [Bb][F]gratitude [C7][F]sincere,
[x]Thanks [C]to Thee, [x]O [F]loving Savior,
[F]For [Bb]redemption through [F]Thy blood.
[x]Breathe [F]upon [x]us, [Bb]Holy Spirit,
[C]Sweetly [F]draw [Bb]us [F]near [C7]to [F]God.
{end_of_verse}
